# Git never converts line endings in this repository, on any platform, no
# matter what a user's core.autocrlf is set to.
#
# Linux is the primary das2C development platform and the Windows tools in
# use read LF.  More importantly, some files break if a single byte changes:
# das text streams (*.d3t, *.d2t) carry header byte counts such as
# |Sx||1153|, so a CR added to each line invalidates the stream, and test
# golds (*.info, *.csv) are compared byte for byte.  Files stored with CRLF,
# such as the .bat scripts that cmd.exe expects, keep it.
#
# -text only turns off conversion; git still treats files as text for diff
# and merge.
* -text
